@startuml authentication_flow
!theme plain

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
  FontColor #1A237E
  FontSize 13
}

skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  BorderColor #E65100
}

actor "User\n(Browser)" as User #FFF3E0
participant "SAML Service\nProvider (SP)" as SP #E8F5E9
participant "SAML-OIDC Bridge\n(Identity SAML Provider)" as Bridge #E3F2FD
database "PostgreSQL" as DB #F3E5F5
participant "Ory Hydra\n(OIDC Provider)" as Hydra #FFF8E1
participant "Ory Kratos\n(Login UI)" as Kratos #FFEBEE

title **Identity SAML Provider — End-to-End Authentication Flow**

== SP-Initiated SAML Authentication ==

User -> SP: 1. Access protected resource
activate SP #C8E6C9

SP -> SP: Detect unauthenticated user
SP --> User: 2. Redirect with **SAMLRequest**\n(HTTP-Redirect / HTTP-POST)
deactivate SP

User -> Bridge: 3. GET /saml/sso?SAMLRequest=...&RelayState=...
activate Bridge #BBDEFB

Bridge -> Bridge: Parse SAMLRequest\n(crewjam/saml ServeSSO)

== Session Check ==

Bridge -> Bridge: 4. Check for "saml_session" cookie

Bridge -> DB: Lookup session by cookie value
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: No valid session found
deactivate DB

== OIDC Authentication via Hydra ==

Bridge -> Bridge: 5. Store pending SAML request\n(in-memory, keyed by request ID)
Bridge --> User: Redirect to Hydra authorization URL\nstate = requestID[:relayState]\nscopes = openid, email, profile
deactivate Bridge

User -> Hydra: 6. GET /oauth2/auth?scope=openid+email+profile&state=...
activate Hydra #FFF9C4

Hydra --> User: Redirect to login UI
deactivate Hydra

User -> Kratos: Present credentials
activate Kratos #FFCDD2
Kratos -> Kratos: Validate credentials
Kratos --> User: Authentication success
deactivate Kratos

User -> Hydra: Complete consent
activate Hydra #FFF9C4
Hydra --> User: Redirect to /saml/callback\nwith authorization **code** + **state**
deactivate Hydra

User -> Bridge: 7. GET /saml/callback?code=...&state=...
activate Bridge #BBDEFB

Bridge -> Hydra: Exchange code for tokens\n(POST /oauth2/token)
activate Hydra #FFF9C4
Hydra --> Bridge: Access Token + **ID Token**
deactivate Hydra

Bridge -> Bridge: Verify ID Token, extract claims

note right of Bridge
  Claims extracted:
  * sub (subject identifier)
  * email
  * name
  * groups
  * all raw claims (for per-SP mapping)
end note

Bridge -> DB: 8. Save session (10 min TTL)
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: OK
deactivate DB

Bridge -> Bridge: Recover pending SAML request from state

Bridge --> User: Set "saml_session" cookie\nRedirect to /saml/sso\nwith original SAMLRequest
deactivate Bridge

== SAML Response Generation (Second Pass) ==

User -> Bridge: 9. GET /saml/sso?SAMLRequest=...&RelayState=...
activate Bridge #BBDEFB

Bridge -> Bridge: Check "saml_session" cookie - found

Bridge -> DB: Lookup session - valid
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: Session with user claims
deactivate DB

Bridge -> DB: Apply per-SP attribute mapping\n(if configured)
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: Mapped session
deactivate DB

Bridge -> DB: Lookup SP metadata\n(ACS URL, binding)
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: SP descriptor
deactivate DB

Bridge -> Bridge: Build & sign SAML Response

Bridge --> User: 10. Auto-submit form with SAMLResponse\n(HTTP-POST binding)
deactivate Bridge

== Session Established at SP ==

User -> SP: 11. POST /saml/acs\n(SAMLResponse + RelayState)
activate SP #C8E6C9
SP -> SP: Validate signature, create session
SP --> User: Redirect to original resource
deactivate SP

User -> SP: Access granted
activate SP #C8E6C9
SP --> User: Protected resource content
deactivate SP

@enduml
